---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import PipelineDiagram from '../../components/diagrams/PipelineDiagram.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Data engineering pipeline"
  summary="A batch pipeline that lands, validates and models 2.1M rows a day into a warehouse that downstream dashboards and models can trust."
  metaDescription="Data engineering pipeline by Quoc Nguyen: Airflow-orchestrated ELT with dbt models and 120+ data-quality checks gating every layer."
  stack={['Airflow/Dagster', 'dbt', 'SQL', 'Docker', 'CI']}
  nextSteps={[
    'TODO: honest next step — e.g. move high-churn sources to incremental loads.',
    'TODO: honest next step — e.g. publish data-quality SLOs to consumers.',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="links">
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">live demo — TODO: url</span>
    <span class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.04em] text-muted">repo — TODO: url</span>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      TODO: replace with the real problem story. The shape of it: the numbers people make
      decisions from were assembled by hand from exports, so every report was slow to
      produce and impossible to reproduce.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted">
      The quiet failure mode is worse than the visible one: a source schema drifts, a load
      silently drops rows, and dashboards keep rendering confidently wrong numbers. The
      pipeline treats data quality as a first-class output — every layer is gated by checks
      that fail loudly instead.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="diagram"><PipelineDiagram /></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="diagram-caption">
    Fig. 02 — Sources are ingested and modeled in the warehouse; the DAG orchestrates
    every step and quality checks gate every model.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="evaluation">
    <div class="max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted">Measured</span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink">
        For a pipeline, evaluation means reliability: data freshness against an SLA, the
        pass rate of quality checks per run, and how much data actually lands per day.
      </p>
      <span class="mt-8 block font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted"
        >Eval design</span
      >
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        TODO: real details. Template: checks run at every DAG boundary — schema and volume
        on landing, nulls, uniqueness and referential integrity after each dbt model — with
        two severity tiers: blocking failures stop the DAG, warnings page but let it run.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid max-w-[720px] grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">2.1M</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Rows / day
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">38</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          DAG tasks
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-mono text-[30px] leading-none font-medium text-ink">120+</div>
        <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">
          Quality checks
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[720px] overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
        <caption class="caption mb-4 text-left text-muted">Checks by family</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">Check family</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">Count</th>
            <th class="py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.06em] uppercase text-muted">On failure</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-mono text-[13px] text-ink">
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Schema / contract</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">TODO</td>
            <td class="py-3">block</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Freshness / volume</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">TODO</td>
            <td class="py-3">block</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-grid">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Distribution drift</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-muted">TODO</td>
            <td class="py-3">warn</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-[60ch]">
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-muted"
        >What failed → what was fixed</span
      >
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        TODO: the real failure story. Template: backfills initially double-counted rows in
        partially loaded partitions — switching loads to idempotent partition swaps made
        reruns safe, which is what makes the daily volume number trustworthy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectLayout>
